.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="James Musher (1969) grouped molecules such as \mathrm{PCl_5}, \mathrm{SF_6}, \mathrm{ClF_3} and the xenon fluorides into one class: hypervalent molecules, whose central main-group atom appears to hold more than the eight electrons of Lewis&#x27;s octet. Counting the Lewis electrons around the central atom (two per bond plus two per lone pair) gives 10 or 12 for all of them.">

